examples/gspo_trainer/README.md:1:# GSPO (Group Sequence Policy Optimization)
examples/gspo_trainer/README.md:3:GSPO is a GRPO-family policy-loss variant that aggregates the IS-ratio at the sequence level (`seq-mean-token-mean`) and uses a very tight clip window. It is especially useful for large MoE models.
examples/cispo_trainer/README.md:1:# CISPO
examples/cispo_trainer/README.md:3:CISPO (Clipped IS-weight Policy Optimization) is a policy-loss variant that decouples the lower/upper clip ratios to stabilize IS-ratio-weighted updates, used in MiniMax-M1.
